1.2B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $311M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.50\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 84% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 13% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 64% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 51% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Kyivstar Gr